# Project docs (humans and agents)

Before non-trivial work in this repo:

1. Open [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) and pick the matching **concern** doc (data, billing, authentication-and-authorization, conventions, …).
2. **Match installed official docs** — for every dependency, use docs for the version in `package.json` / `node_modules/<pkg>/package.json` (never training data alone). Procedure + lookup: [`docs/conventions.md`](docs/conventions.md#match-installed-official-docs). Next also ships guides in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — see `AGENTS.md`.
3. **Concern over vendor** — durable docs are named for the concern; Stripe/Clerk/Query live *inside* those pages.
4. **One tool per job** — no parallel stacks for the same purpose; replace only if the other tool dominates. [`docs/conventions.md`](docs/conventions.md#one-tool-per-job) · testing split: [`docs/testing.md`](docs/testing.md#what-to-test-where).
5. Code comments and rules should point at a **file** (e.g. `docs/billing.md`), not at another doc’s section titles.

Topic-specific rules (e.g. billing) still apply when their globs match; they do not replace this index.
